    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.08,
    "rationale": "I re-read the 18 h aliquot at three dilutions. Each reading was multiplied by its dilution factor to give an undiluted-equivalent OD. The 10x reads were 0.168 and 0.163, giving about 1.65. The 3x read was 0.538, giving about 1.61. The 30x read was 0.050, giving about 1.50. The undiluted reading was 1.55. All four estimates fall within about ±5% of each other and show no trend with dilution. If the reader were saturating at about 1.6, the diluted samples would have given much higher values. The plateau from about 7 h onward therefore looks like real stationary phase. Biomass is at the level the readings indicate, perhaps 3–6% higher, which is within noise."
